{
  "_readme": [
    "Copy this file to cdk.context.json and fill in your own vault.",
    "cdk.context.json is gitignored because these values name real",
    "infrastructure. They are not credentials. The Skyflow API key never",
    "appears here and lives only in Secrets Manager.",
    "Keys beginning with an underscore are ignored by CDK, so they are safe",
    "to leave in place after you copy the file."
  ],

  "_skyflowVaultUrl": [
    "Open your vault in the Skyflow console. The URL of the vault page is",
    "https://<cluster>.vault.skyflowapis.com and <cluster> is a short",
    "alphanumeric id unique to your account. Copy the whole origin with no",
    "trailing slash and no path."
  ],
  "skyflowVaultUrl": "https://<cluster>.vault.skyflowapis.com",

  "_skyflowVaultId": [
    "Also in the Skyflow console on the vault page. It is a 32 character",
    "hexadecimal string. The console labels it Vault ID."
  ],
  "skyflowVaultId": "<vault-id>",

  "_nextStep": [
    "Two more things need your values before a first deploy.",
    "1. Store the Skyflow API key:",
    "   aws secretsmanager create-secret --name skyflow/detect-api-key",
    "     --secret-string '<SKYFLOW_API_KEY>' --region us-east-1",
    "2. Point files.destinations in gateway/interceptor/config/policy.json at",
    "   a table and columns that exist in your vault. It ships as",
    "   table1.{entity}_entity. A table that does not exist fails the Skyflow",
    "   run with '<name> schema not found' rather than failing validation,",
    "   because only Skyflow knows your schema."
  ]
}
